jobs.description:
Are you accurate and do you enjoy working with different materials and machines? For our client in Waalwijk, we are looking for a Production Employee for the Preparation Department. Together with a team of four colleagues, you will transform bulk materials into precisely sized components used in the production of custom-made sandwich panels.

What will you do?

You will work with materials such as foam, wood, and composite. Using production lists, you will cut and calibrate these materials to the required dimensions.

- Adjust materials to the correct thickness using various saws and calibration machines;
- Cut materials to size at your own workstation;
- Calibrate material thickness using a thickness planer;
- Label components according to the production list and sort them onto transport carts;
- Keep your work area clean and organized.

Since every sandwich panel is custom-made, you will work with different production lists and dimensions every day.

What do we expect from you?

- You work accurately and enjoy working as part of a team;
- You can read production lists or are willing to learn;
- You speak Dutch or English.

Are you an enthusiastic Order Picker with EPT experience, or are you eager to learn? We are looking for motivated candidates to join a modern logistics company in Helmond. As an Order Picker with EPT, you will be responsible for collecting, checking, and moving goods throughout the warehouse. Your work ensures that customer orders are processed accurately and shipped on time.

Your responsibilities:

- Picking customer orders using a handheld scanner;
- Checking orders before shipment;
- Moving goods and pallets using an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT);
- Wrapping, labeling, and scanning pallets;
- Performing Value Added Services (VAS) activities;
- Supporting various warehouse and logistics processes;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized working environment.

Working Hours in the regular day shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule applies:

- 06:00 AM – 03:00 PM
- 03:00 PM – 12:00 AM

- Has experience operating an EPT or is willing to learn;
- Fulltime available;
- Is flexible regarding tasks and working hours;
- Performs well under pressure;
- Enjoys working in a team;
- Has a good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Has a proactive and hands-on attitude.

Are you looking for a job at a manufacturing company with varied responsibilities? This is a position as an operator working in a 5-shift rotation in the packaging department. In this role, you’ll work as a production worker in a 5-shift rotation at a company in Ittervoort. Your daily tasks will include:

- Operating the (packaging) machine and troubleshooting malfunctions during the packaging process;
- Operating the mixer, where raw materials are blended;
- Working in accordance with HACCP guidelines to ensure food safety;
- Restocking products using a forklift.

You will work in a 5-shift rotation, with the following schedules: 1:45 p.m. – 10:15 p.m., 9:45 p.m. – 6:15 a.m., 5:45 a.m. – 2:15 p.m. (8,5 hours per day).

You can work in various roles, including loader, mixer, filler, and packer. You’ll learn all of this on the job. 

- MBO-level work and thinking skills, preferably in the field of food or engineering. Do you happen to have experience in the food industry? Then you have an edge!;
- Experience operating machinery;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English for safety regulations;
- You have an eye for detail, and you’re also flexible and able to handle stress.

Do you have a forklift certification? That’s a definite plus!

As an Order Picker, you help make sure customers receive their orders quickly and correctly.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders using a handheld scanner;
- Checking products and quantities;
- Packing and preparing orders for shipment;
- Placing products in the correct warehouse locations;
- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Helping colleagues when needed;
- Keeping the warehouse clean and safe.

Working Hours

You will work 40 hours per week.

You can choose between:

Morning Shift

- 07:00 AM to 04:00 PM

Evening Shift

- 04:00 PM to 01:00 AM

- MBO level or similar working and thinking level;
- Motivated and willing to work hard;
- Accurate and reliable;
- Able to speak Dutch or English;
- Physically fit and comfortable with warehouse work;
- Own transportation (car, scooter, moped, or e-bike);
- Warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

Your responsibilities will include:

- Loading and unloading goods;
- Moving and stacking pallets;
- Processing and handling products within the warehouse;
- Lifting and moving boxes weighing up to 23 kg;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized workspace.

You will also perform various Value Added Services (VAS), such as:

- Applying stickers and labels to products;
- Repacking and packaging items;
- Preparing products for shipment;
- Inflating and preparing sports and recreational products for distribution.

You will primarily work in a day shift from 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule will apply:

- 06:00 AM – 03:00 PM
- 03:00 PM – 12:00 AM
- A 12.5% shift allowance applies during these periods.

You are someone who enjoys physical work and likes to stay active throughout the day.

Additionally, you:

- Are physically fit and enjoy hands-on work;
- Are available to work fulltime and can commit to a fixed work schedule;
- Are flexible and willing to work shifts during peak in July till October;
- Have an EPT certificate or are willing to obtain one;
- Live in Helmond or nearby;
- Have a good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Are motivated and reliable.

We’re looking for a reach truck operator who is skilled at driving this type of equipment for a dynamic organization in the Echt region. In this role, you’ll be responsible for handling incoming and outgoing goods using a reach truck. Does working in a clean, well-organized facility energize you? This permanent position offers you job security on the day shift!

Duties:

- Placing pallets of products on shelves using a single-deep or double-deep reach truck;
- Picking orders; 
- Assisting with loading containers; 
- Supporting all logistical tasks as they arise.

You’ll spend most of your time operating the reach truck, so it’s important that you have experience with this type of logistics vehicle. Do you see yourself in this role? Don’t hesitate—read on!

This is a day shift position from 6:00 AM to 3:00 PM, Monday through Friday. 

- Experience operating a reach truck and a certificate demonstrating that you possess the qualities of a good reach truck operator;
- You speak Dutch, English, or German.

Are you someone who enjoys physical work and are you looking for a full-time position in day shift? Then we have a great opportunity for you! For Dorel Juvenile in Helmond, we are looking for a motivated Loader & Unloader who is ready to roll up their sleeves.Together with your colleagues, you will ensure that goods are processed correctly and efficiently. You will stay active throughout the day and play an important role in the logistics process.

What will you do?

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Checking and processing incoming goods;
- Packing and preparing outgoing shipments for dispatch;
- Storing products in the correct warehouse locations;
- Assisting with stock counts and inventory management;
- Maintaining a neat, safe, and organized working environment.

- You speak Dutch or English;
- You are physically fit and enjoy active work;
- You can travel independently to Helmond;
- You are available for day shifts from 08:00 AM to 04:30 PM;
- Experience in logistics is a plus, but not required.

As an Order Picker, you play an important role in the warehouse operation. Together with your colleagues, you make sure orders are processed efficiently and correctly.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders using a handheld scanner;
- Preparing orders for shipment;
- Operating an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT);
- Loading and unloading goods;
- Checking products for accuracy and completeness;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized workplace.

Thanks to a structured onboarding program, you'll quickly learn all aspects of the job.

- Are available for day shifts from 08:00 AM to 04:30 PM;
- Have a basic understanding of Dutch and/or English;
- Enjoy physical and active work;
- Work accurately and responsibly;
- Are motivated and eager to learn.

Previous logistics experience is a plus, but not required.
